# What the server image build leaves out of its context (src/). Docker reads this file because it sits next to the
# Dockerfile and carries its name, so it applies to "docker build -f adapters/azure/Product.Azure.Server/Dockerfile ."
# without a .dockerignore at the root of src/.
#
# Build output from the machine that runs the build: the image restores and builds from source, and a local obj folder
# would hand the container restore results with this machine's paths.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vs/
**/*.user

# Local state that must never reach an image layer: SQLite files from local runs, Azure Functions local settings and
# Azure Developer CLI environment values.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/local.settings.json
**/.azure/
**/.env
**/.env.*
